@startuml Google OAuth 2.0 Desktop Flow

actor User
participant Browser
participant Google
participant "Client App" as Client
participant "CDA Server" as CDA
participant "ECU Simulator" as ECU

== Phase 1: Authorization ==

User -> Client : Request access
Client -> Client : Generate auth URL with\nclient_id, scopes, redirect_uri
Client -> User : Display auth URL
User -> Browser : Open URL
Browser -> Google : Authorization request
Google -> User : Login & consent screen
User -> Google : Approve access
Google -> Browser : Authorization code
User -> Client : Copy authorization code

== Phase 2: Token Exchange ==

Client -> CDA : POST /oauth/callback\n{code: "auth_code"}
CDA -> Google : Exchange code for tokens\n(client_id, client_secret, code)
Google -> CDA : ID token + access token
CDA -> CDA : Validate ID token (JWKS)
CDA -> Client : {access_token, expires_in}
Client -> Client : Store access_token

== Phase 3: Authenticated API Calls ==

Client -> CDA : GET /components/flxc1000/data/...\nAuthorization: Bearer {token}
CDA -> CDA : Validate JWT signature (Google JWKS)
CDA -> CDA : Extract email from claims
CDA -> CDA : Lookup roles in oauth_roles.toml
CDA -> CDA : Check audience restrictions

alt Access Granted
    CDA -> ECU : UDS Request (22 F1 99)
    ECU -> CDA : UDS Response (62 F1 99 ...)
    CDA -> Client : JSON response with DID data
else Access Denied
    CDA -> Client : 403 Forbidden
end

== Runtime: Reload Roles ==

Client -> CDA : POST /oauth/reload-roles
CDA -> CDA : Re-read oauth_roles.toml
CDA -> Client : {id: "reload-roles", data: {success: true}}

@enduml